enchilada: MSS: read-only QMI probe of DMS, UIM and NAS (qmiprobe=1 with mss>=7; cellular round 1)

logs/cellular/plan.md milestone 1 (SIM read). boot38 (mss=7) showed the modem announcing DMS 0x02, NAS 0x03, UIM 0x0b, WMS 0x05, VOICE 0x09 v2, WDS 0x01, WDA 0x1a and ~40 others once rmtfs/TFTP/pd-mapper are served. With boot-arg qmiprobe=1 (and mss>=7, else idle), a QMI client on apps port 0x4005 waits until DMS, UIM and NAS have all been announced (NEW_SERVER, forgotten on DEL_SERVER), then 5 s later asks, one request at a time (3 s timeout each, as qmicli would), only "get" messages with no TLVs: DMS 0x23 revision, 0x25 serial numbers (IMEI logged as its TAC + '*'), 0x2d operating mode (+ offline reason, hardware restricted), 0x3c ICCID (6 chars kept), 0x43 IMSI (MCC+MNC kept); UIM 0x2f card status (per slot card state, UPIN, error code; per application type, state, perso, PIN1/PUK1 retries; AIDs not logged); NAS 0x24 serving system (registration, CS/PS attach, radio, PLMN) and 0x4f signal info (GSM/WCDMA/LTE/NR). The pass runs again 60 s later (the card may still be initializing at the first) and a summary line closes the watch. Replies are matched by node, port, transaction and message id; every length is bounded by the QMI header and TLV lengths (qmi_tlv). Nothing is set: the modem stays in the operating mode it booted in (no DMS SET_OPERATING_MODE, so no RF), no UIM slot switch or provisioning session, no NAS register/selection, no indication registration, and rmtfs keeps dropping every EFS write; no partition is written. Over QRTR each port is a QMI client, so no QMI CTL client-id allocation is needed. Without qmiprobe, or with mss<=6, behaviour is unchanged.

